<span id="S5.T3.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom" style="--ltx-bg-color:#62BC7A;"><span style="visibility:hidden">xx</span></span> <math id="S5.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>90</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 90</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="S5.T3.8.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best</span>)  
<span id="S5.T3.8.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom" style="--ltx-bg-color:#A1CF7E;"><span style="visibility:hidden">xx</span></span> <math id="S5.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80\sim 90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>80</mn><mo>∼</mo><mn>90</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80\sim 90</annotation></semantics></math>  
<span id="S5.T3.8.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom" style="--ltx-bg-color:#DFE282;"><span style="visibility:hidden">xx</span></span> <math id="S5.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="70\sim 80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo>∼</mo><mn>80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">70\sim 80</annotation></semantics></math>  
<span id="S5.T3.8.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FCD07E;"><span style="visibility:hidden">xx</span></span> <math id="S5.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60\sim 70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>∼</mo><mn>70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60\sim 70</annotation></semantics></math>  
<span id="S5.T3.8.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F99C74;"><span style="visibility:hidden">xx</span></span> <math id="S5.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50\sim 60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>∼</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50\sim 60</annotation></semantics></math>  
<span id="S5.T3.8.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_phantom" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7686A;"><span style="visibility:hidden">xx</span></span> <math id="S5.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 50</annotation></semantics></math> (Bad)</span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate robustness under increasing motion blur by jointly adjusting illumination and exposure time (Tab. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.5 Motion Blur Performance ‣ 5 Experiment ‣ E-VLA: Event-augmented Vision-Language-Action Model forDark and Blurred Scenes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Under mild blur, methods are comparable. As blur increases, image-only performance drops sharply: at 300 ms, overlay improves Pick-Place from 40% to 90% and Sorting from 52.5% to 72.5%, while the event adapter reaches 85%/85%. Under severe blur (1000 ms), image-only falls to 0% (Pick-Place) and 5% (Sorting), whereas overlay achieves 20%/32.5% and the event adapter further improves Pick-Place to 25% (Sorting: 32.5%). All models are trained without motion-blurred data, indicating gains stem from event sensing (high temporal resolution + recent-count windowing) rather than blur-specific adaptation, and mitigating the low-light/exposure trade-off of frame imaging.</p>
</div>
</section>
